{
    "background_story": "Fatima was a talented artist with a unique style that captivated everyone who laid eyes on her work. Despite her incredible skill, she struggled to promote herself, often downplaying her accomplishments and selling her art for far less than it was worth. Her friends and family would often encourage her to raise her prices, but Fatima's humble nature made her uncomfortable with self-promotion. As a result, she became known as the 'underseller' of the local art scene. One day, a prominent art critic stumbled upon her work and was blown away by her talent. He wrote a glowing review, highlighting Fatima's modesty and generosity as much as her artistic prowess. Overnight, her studio was flooded with requests, and she was finally able to command the prices her work deserved. Fatima's story serves as a reminder that sometimes, it takes others to recognize our worth before we can recognize it ourselves.",
